        <span itemprop="definition">was produced in the same manner as in Example 1, except that a non-woven fabric with a thickness of 10  ⁇ m, made of a mixture of polyethylene terephthalate fibers with a melting point of 260° C. and polyethylene terephthalate fibers with a melting point of 130° C., and on which 80 g/m 2 of polyethylene grains with a melting point of 120° C. were retained instead of the PTFE grains with a melting point of 320° C., was used.</span>
